==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang}} ''[[hæþen]]'', akin to [[heath]] on the moor, the poor, 'wild' countryside; cognate with Dutch [[heiden]], German [[Heide]].

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|iːðən}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Not adhering to an [[Abrahamic]] [[religion]]; [[pagan]].
# {{by extension}} Uncultured; uncivilized; savage, [[philistine]].
# Pertaining to Germanic currents of [[neo-paganism]] known as [[Heathenry]].

